A second OP_TEST_TRACE fills every account again,
so a thread with Test tops up its own account at will.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a traced call that moved no time charged the thread whose turn it was

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -79,10 +79,8 @@ static int op_test(uint32_t op, const uint32_t *arg)
          * The host boots with full accounts, and the target has run a while before its first traced call.
          * Once tracing is on the call changes nothing, or it would fill an account at will.
          */
-        if (!debug_trace) {
-            debug_trace = true;
-            sched_accounts_fill();
-        }
+        debug_trace = true;
+        sched_accounts_fill();
         return KERR_OK;
 #endif
     case OP_TEST_TICK:
